.Dd August 22, 2026
.Dt PQFREEBSD 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pqfreebsd
.Nd post-quantum access control: ledger evidence and repaired A_D
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
extends
.Xr pqac 7 .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mandoc -T pdf pqfreebsd.7 > pqfreebsd.pdf
mandoc -T lint pqfreebsd.7
.Ed
.Sh ABSTRACT
.Xr pqac 7
argued that
.Em A_D ,
.Em A_M ,
and MMU translation are quantum-adversary-stable mediation on a von Neumann
.Fx
defender: not post-quantum cryptography, not a quantum ISA.
T1 and T2 are implemented by
.Nm freebsd-mac-grok .
.Pp
What the slogans omitted is Anderson's third property and the residual
access matrix.
.Nm
packages those as morphisms.
.Em pqledger
is a filesystem-level Integrity Evidence chain.
.Em pqdac
is a restricted
.Em A_D
established at create and repaired on drift.
Neither is Kyber.
Neither is Faraday.
.Pp
A further requirement of the system is
.Em not
implemented in this pass: the data itself must have integrity that can
be confirmed, to a certain extent
.Pq T10, Nm pqconfirm .
.Sh THESES
Deniable separately.
T1–T5 remain
.Xr pqac 7 .
.Bl -tag -width T10xx
.It T6
Unrestricted
.Em A_D
is an HRU protection system; safety is undecidable.
A restricted specification
.Pq path-regex to owner, group, mode, inherit
plus a repair morphism is a different relation: intended
.Em A_D
is restored; residual owner-grants are bounded in duration.
This does not make
.Em A_D
into
.Em A_M .
.It T7
.Xr mac 4
approximates complete mediation and isolation.
Verifiability is not supplied.
A hash-chained ledger of vnode, label, and policy-morphism events is the
monitor's evidence.
The ledger object is high in
.Em L .
Tampering is a hash-collision problem
.Pq Grover halves the bits; production uses SHA-512 or SHA-3 .
That is
.Em A_auth
of the evidence, not of the subject.
The suite still does not
.Xr kldload 8
Kyber.
.It T8
Dynamic establishment is the create-time morphism.
Repair is the restore morphism when actual is not intended.
.Xr setfsmac 8
first-match and DAC first-match are combinators, not lattice operations.
Conjunction with
.Em A_M
is still not a product of proofs.
Optional prevention
.Pq Xr ugidfw 8
is a different module with a different proof
.Pq empty ruleset is allow-all .
.It T9
The ledger daemon is a subject.
If
.Em O
factors through it, T4 applies.
The ledger is not Faraday, not a naming retrofit, and not a secrecy lattice.
Recovery remains inside the isolation claim.
.It T10
.Pq required; not this pass
.Em A_M
constrains who may write.
The ledger records that a write occurred.
Neither lets a later subject confirm that the bits they read are the bits
that were written.
.Xr zfs 8
checksums detect silent corruption inside the pool; they are not a
subject-visible confirmation API.
A content digest, or a Merkle over the labeled store, bound to a ledger
checkpoint, is confirmable to the extent of the hash.
Grover halves the bits.
This is not Faraday and not information-theoretic.
Next skill:
.Nm pqconfirm .
.It T11
.Pq required; not this pass
A PQ-stable monitor interpreting RSA-signed code is a forged policy,
correctly enforced.
T2 is mediation, not a cryptographic game.
The system is not therefore post-quantum secure.
Kernel, klds, pkg, policy, and
.Xr zfs 8
send streams are code, or code-shaped.
If they are unsigned, or signed with RSA/ECC, Shor forges the input to
.Em A_M .
Authentication here is of code, not of credentials.
Redundancy is two independent reductions: ML-DSA
.Pq FIPS 204, lattices
and SLH-DSA
.Pq FIPS 205, hashes
— not two disks.
Fletcher, RAID-Z, and AES-at-rest are not a second signature.
Held:
.Nm pqcode ,
.Nm pqzfs .
.It T12
.Pq gated; TPM not this pass
Once the operator attests they are sufficiently satisfied that the system is
post-quantum hardened to the degree that gives them a sense of security, the
umbrella offers
.Cm oneboot :
the splash name becomes
.Nm pqfreebsd ;
the beastie is replaced by the shield
.Pq the armor of God ;
the loader is taken off the unsigned GENERIC path only as far as this pass
can close.
TPM and measured boot are not this pass.
Default is no.
Do not rebrand a box you do not yet trust.
Branding is not a second signature family.
.It T13
After install, the operator must see that POLICY, SUITE, DAC, ugidfw, login
labels, MAC overlays, and the splash agree; must propagate a change through
all of them at once; and must read the diff of successive iterations.
Consistency is a predicate over that conjunction, not a product of proofs.
Each propagation is a named revision whose catalog hash is chained and
recorded in the ledger.
An audit that cannot show what changed is not an audit.
.Cm oneaudit ,
.Cm onepropagate .
.It T14
Claims degrade by conjunct, not as a product.
A missing or stranded protocol weakens only the claims that named it.
If the box cannot securely transport the Integrity Evidence to another host
and have that host validate the store, the off-host IE claim is degraded.
Write-up, local chain, repaired A_D, successive policy, and the splash are
not thereby false.
A deployment that includes and enables that module, and adheres to its
protocol, keeps those claims in full.
Silent (module not included) is not degraded (module included, protocol unmet).
Do not report the suite as a single bit.
.El
.Sh PRAXIS
.Ss Genesis is a named record
An empty chain is not evidence.
The first record names the policy hash, the dataset, and the hash.
.Xr audit 4
is the in-band source;
.Pa /var/audit
is not the chain.
Rotation appends a checkpoint record.
Rewrite is a bug.
.Ss Label the ledger before enforce
A high dataset unlabeled at
.Cm enforce
is an unlabeled hole
.Pq empty interpretation .
Overlays precede the official PLM because the combinator is first-match.
.Ss Repair bounds duration, not the syscall
.Xr chmod 2
still succeeds in repair mode.
A concurrent reader may see the drifted mode.
Say so.
.Cm prevent
is
.Xr mac_bsdextended 4
generated from the same spec.
Do not rest a proof on aux covering xattrs
.Pq PR 178667 .
.Ss Restricted language
No arbitrary grant verbs in the spec.
That is the HRU cut.
.Ss Event integrity is not payload integrity
The ledger confirms an op happened.
It does not confirm the bytes of a file.
Do not pretend a scrub discharges T10.
.Ss Sign the bits that run
.Xr pkg 8
RSA, unsigned
.Xr kldload 8 ,
unsigned
.Nm zfs send ,
unsigned policy files: each is an
.Em A_auth
of code that T2 set aside.
Hybrid ML-DSA + SLH-DSA is the redundancy.
Do not wrap ZFS keys in RSA.
Do not call the system post-quantum secure while those rows are classical
or empty.
